.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 948 AM PST Thu Nov 19 2026

Weak surface low pressure has moved inland allowing winds to turn
light NW for key terminals like SFO/OAK. Expect numerous showers
to continue today and through much of the 24 hour taf period with
persistent NWerly onshore wind flow and steep lapse rates aloft.
Isolated t-storms possible and small hail will be a key threat
with any showers and t-storms over the next 24 hours. Models keep
-shra activity going at least through 18-19z Friday for most Bay Area
 terminals.

Vicinity of SFO...Winds have turned NW. Scattered showers to
continue through at least midday Friday with periods of VFR/IFR
cigs as cells pass through the region.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Numerous showers to continue the next 24
hours with persistent NW low level flow over the Monterey Bay
region bringing steady showers over KMRY through at least midday
Friday. Slightly less activity for KSNS where southeast winds may
redevelop early Friday morning.

