.MARINE...
(Today through Tuesday)
Issued at 1030 AM PST Thu Nov 19 2026

A 1006 mb surface low has moved inland over the San Francisco Bay
with increasing northwest winds along with showers and isolated
thunderstorms today and into Friday morning. Seas will subside by
early Friday as the storm system exits the region. Another weak
front will pass through the waters later Saturday into Sunday with
a brief lull Monday before more wet weather approaches the region
during the middle of next week along with another large swell set
that will coincide with the king tides.

